:: Orphanage Loft Doren
<<effects>><<set $location to "park">><<set $outside to 1>>

You arrive at the woodshop in the community garden. Doren dons protective gear, then helps you with yours, before explaining the construction plan. <<He>> begins cutting the panels using the measurements <<he>> took, sending wood dust flying everywhere.
<br><br>
Next, <<he>> guides you through constructing the base cabinets, attaching each panel with wood glue and screws. Before driving in the screws, <<he>> drills and countersinks pilot holes to prevent splitting or damaging the material. As you spread glue with your finger, <<he>> builds a toe-kick base for comfort. Then, <<he>> uses rails, stiles, and centre panels to make the drawer fronts while you stain the wood surfaces and seal them with a sprayer.
<br><br>
The face frames are made from plywood with iron-on edge banding to conceal the exposed layers. <<He>> heats the veneer edging with an iron set hot, slowly bonding the strip to the plywood before pressing it firmly into place with a scrap piece of wood. Once the adhesive cools, <<he>> trims away the excess with a utility knife and sands the edges smooth until they blend seamlessly with the surface.
<br><br>
Finally, the two of you pack up and return to the loft.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Orphanage Loft Doren 2]]>><<set $loft_doren to 1>><<set $loft_upgrade += 1>><</link>>

:: Orphanage Loft Doren 2
<<effects>><<set $location to "home">><<set $outside to 0>>
Doren calls a friend of <<his>> to help move the woodwork up the loft. Once there, <<he>> secures the toe kick base into the wall studs and floor. The cabinets are positioned on top of the base and fastened to both the wall studs, and the frame.
<br><br>
After the lower cabinets are installed, you work together to assemble and mount the tall vertical shelving units. <<He>> uses a level and wood shims to keep everything aligned.
<br><br>
The structure is complete, <<he>> attaches the face frames to the front of the cabinets using wood glue and brad nails. All nail holes and joints are filled with wood filler and sanded smooth.
<br><br>
<<He>> clears away the dust with a vacuum for you to apply caulk to all the joints. Then, you both put on respirators before priming and painting the reading nook with a spray gun.
<br><br>
Following <<his>> instructions, you install the drawer faces carefully, using playing cards as spacers to maintain even gaps around all edges.
<br><br>
To finish it up, you place a plywood plank over a thick foam, wrap them in a thick fabric, then staple it tightly to make an upholstered cushion. Doren throws pillows into the seating area, then places a reading lamp to the side, a soft rug in the middle, then the toe kick.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Orphanage Loft Doren 3]]>><</link>>

:: Orphanage Loft Doren 3
<<effects>>
<<wearProp "open storybook">>
Doren claps <<his>> hands together. "Alright!" <<He>> pauses to admire the handiwork. "Oh. The books!"
<br><br>
You open the boxes. One is filled with books. Novels, comics, newspapers, magazines, and reference books. Another is filled with bookmarks, flash cards, stationery and craft supplies.
<br><br>
"Those are helpful resources to study. Knowledge is power, after all," <<he>> says, opening a box full of decorations. "Can't forget about these, either. A welcoming space to learn is also very important."
<br><br>
You and Doren chat while arranging books and decorations on the bookshelf. Together, you create a miniature diorama with lighting, music, and motion sensors, and display it with the books. Finally, you two finish the reading nook up with garlands, hanging paper butterflies and fairy lights.
<br><br>
Resting <<his>> hands on <<his>> waist, Doren beholds the reading nook and smiles proudly. "Good job, <<lass>>. All done. High five!" You give <<him>> a high five.
<br><br>
<<link [[Thank <<him>>|Orphanage Loft Doren Thank]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Thank and hug <<him>>|Orphanage Loft Doren Thank]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>

:: Orphanage Loft Doren Thank
<<effects>>

<<switch $speech_attitude>>
	<<case "meek">>"Thank you so much," you say. "I couldn't have done it without you."
	<<case "bratty">>"Thanks," you say. "This will keep them educated."
	<<default>> "Thank you," you say. "You've been a great help."
<</switch>>
<<if $phase is 2>>
	<br><br>
	You
	<<switch $speech_attitude>>
		<<case "meek">>shyly opens your arms for
		<<case "bratty">>pulls <<him>> into
		<<default>>opens your arms for
	<</switch>>
	a hug, which is met with a soft chuckle as <<he>> returns it.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Of course I'd help. It's great that you've set up this reading nook for the orphans. I'm also glad you asked for my help." Doren beams at you. "I'm proud of you, <<lass>>."
<br><br>
"I've got to go return the tools now. See ya later, <<lass>>." <<He>> waves you goodbye before <<he>> leaves.
<br><br>
<<endevent>>
